ath11k: nss: keep unsupported radios on the host data path

ath11k_nss_setup() returns -ENOTSUPP when the radio has no wifili target
type, and its caller treats that as a fatal pdev error:

  ath11k b00a040.wifi: NSS Offload not supported for this HW
  ath11k b00a040.wifi: failed to setup nss driver interface-524
  ath11k b00a040.wifi: failed to create pdev core: -524
  ath11k b00a040.wifi: failed to wait wlan mode request (mode 4): -110
  ath11k b00a040.wifi: qmi failed to send wlan mode off: -110   (repeating)

so the radio never comes up at all and its QMI teardown spins. On
IPQ5018 this is the QCN6122 pdev: the NSS series knows the built-in
radio (ATH11K_HW_IPQ5018_HW10) but never learned that chip, while the
QCN6122 support came in as a separate series.

nss.enabled is per ath11k_base and each multipd radio has its own, so
the radio can simply be dropped to the host data path while the others
keep their offload. Do that for both "no target type" and "NSS support
disabled", the latter of which already claimed to fall back but did not.

Measured on GL-B3000 (kernel 6.18.44): with this, the 2.4 GHz radio
registers wifili and the 5 GHz radio comes up host-side.

Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
@@ -3555,13 +3555,26 @@
 
 	target_type = ath11k_nss_get_target_type(ab);
 
-	if (target_type == ATH11K_WIFILI_TARGET_TYPE_UNKNOWN)
-		return -ENOTSUPP;
+	/* A radio the wifili code has no target type for cannot be offloaded.
+	 * Returning an error here fails ath11k_core_qmi_firmware_ready() and
+	 * takes the whole pdev down ("failed to create pdev core: -524"),
+	 * leaving the radio dead and its QMI teardown spinning on -110. Drop
+	 * this radio to the host data path instead - the offload is per
+	 * ath11k_base, so the other radios keep theirs. On IPQ5018 this is
+	 * what the QCN6122 pdev needs: the NSS series knows the built-in
+	 * radio but never learned that chip.
+	 */
+	if (target_type == ATH11K_WIFILI_TARGET_TYPE_UNKNOWN) {
+		ath11k_info(ab, "NSS offload not supported for this hw, using the host data path\n");
+		ab->nss.enabled = false;
+		return 0;
+	}
 
 	/* Verify NSS support is enabled */
 	if (nss_cmn_get_nss_enabled() == false) {
 		ath11k_warn(ab, "NSS offload support disabled, falling back to default mode\n");
-		return -ENOTSUPP;
+		ab->nss.enabled = false;
+		return 0;
 	}
 
 	/* Initialize completion for verifying NSS message response */
